id: pm-rl-sequential
title: Stop predeclared evaluations safely at sequential boundaries
description: "Extend sealed evaluation plans with reviewed sequential stopping. Acceptance: deterministic null and benefit simulations validate the declared error bound; seal the rule before collection; fixed plans preserve behavior; saved checkpoints resume without recounting. Include typed SDK and CLI, compact reports, typed remedies, model-based replay tests, boundary interleavings and read-only public tracker evidence."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-rl#107"
created_at: "2026-10-25T23:52:20.254Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T23:30:51.615Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[53]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T23:52:27.192Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check on current CLI 2026.10.25 and sibling package source/docs: pm-rl-evalplans explicitly seals fixed stopping; core SDK exposes tracker transactions and locks, not sequential statistics; pm-jev owns inference receipts, pm-context context selection, pm-rlm inference recursion. No existing alpha-spending evaluation protocol found. This extends pm-rl evaluation plans, retaining promotion approval and contamination gates. Design: predeclared finite looks over frozen complete correlation units, two-sided Hoeffding alpha spending, reviewed rule identity, immutable append-only checkpoint chain with SDK writer serialization and current provenance checks on every retry. No import/export/sync subsystem or status-name classification is introduced."
  "2026-10-26T00:01:50.075Z",codex-agent,"Implemented reviewed finite-look plans, cumulative immutable checkpoint chaining, advance/resume CLI and promotion bindings. Seeded 10,000-trial null/benefit simulations measured zero false efficacy and zero false futility decisions at the declared 0.05 bound; all 10,000 benefit trials stopped early. Targeted real SDK tests pass for restart, old snapshot retries, changed candidate provenance, futility and exhaustion. A 500-sequence SDK model test is running. Production typecheck, lint, duplication and docstrings pass so far; full npm/Bun release evidence will use CI as instructed."
  "2026-10-26T00:13:48.212Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public tracker validation passed using the installed packed CLI with Git absent from PATH. Public source commit 120e20e160897cabe47920713e1b87b6647b2e85: 107 items, 87 done-role items using the SDK status registry, candidate mean 0.8130841121495327 vs incumbent 0.1869158878504673. One repository remains one unit; exhausted/refuse, no promotion. JSON 853 bytes; TOON 730 bytes; one checkpoint, exact restart, source digest unchanged. Linked pm tests pass 3/3 (five focused regressions, typecheck, lint); configured tracking is disabled, so the receipt is recorded here. Behavioral revert controls: removing uncertainty fails null simulation; returning the requested old checkpoint fails restart/old-input regression; restored implementation passes 2/2. All 29 existing fixed-plan tests pass. No core dependency pins, thresholds or history records changed."
  "2026-10-26T00:14:57.144Z",codex-agent,"Opened ready-for-review PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/107 at 34afb0c. Full isolated-identity npm Node 22/26 and Bun Node 26 release checks are running in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/40248393802. Final-head gate results will be verified before handoff. No merge or release is authorized."
  "2026-10-26T00:23:08.967Z",codex-agent,"Final implementation correction: retain explicit sequential-kind validation at the SDK boundary and pass its typed rule into internal checkpoint reads; fixed-plan advance/resume now return typed stopping refusals. Regression tests pass 4/4 including 22 registration interleavings and 2 publication boundaries. Earlier checkpoint interleavings passed at 34 SDK boundaries. New promotion tests refuse missing or foreign checkpoints. The superseded initial CI run was canceled after this deterministic refusal-path defect was found; cancellation is not gate evidence. Final code-head CI must pass all three complete release checks before handoff. External review has no approval: CodeRabbit skips under repository policy, Sourcery is budget-limited, Greptile trial expired; zero inline findings."
  "2026-10-26T00:32:03.431Z",codex-agent,"Additional concurrency hardening found during final audit: hold native SDK locks on every predecessor checkpoint through dependent checkpoint publication, so an ordinary SDK writer cannot change a predecessor into a foreign record after validation. This prevents a dependent write before returning a skip. A new real-peer test injects the mutation immediately before and after publication, then verifies foreign state is observed after lease release. Superseding the prior code-head CI run; only the eventual complete final-head run will count as gate evidence."
  "2026-10-26T00:34:32.286Z",codex-agent,"Predecessor-race and asynchronous SDK intake tests pass 2/2 on the restored implementation. Removing only predecessor locks makes the real-peer regression fail; restoring them passes. Canonical observations are now copied before asynchronous provenance reads, preventing caller mutation from changing the look or observations after lock selection. Local typecheck, test typecheck, lint, zero-duplication and 416 documented declarations pass. Final release CI will execute the complete 500-sequence model with live SDK state, relationships and custom statuses; previous canceled runs are not acceptance evidence."
  "2026-10-26T07:52:56.803Z",codex-agent,"Orchestrator read-only review blocks PR 107: unvalidated dependency identifiers can reach native lock cleanup before plan rejection. Extending scope to the identifier-validation and state-path confinement class across the package, with real SDK must-allow/must-refuse property coverage, external tripwires, symlink checks and a boundary-validation revert proof. Existing evaluation implementation and prior gate evidence are retained; new code requires a new exact-head npm/Bun gate."
  "2026-10-26T08:13:09.805Z",codex-agent,"Implemented a single strict identifier boundary, SDK-delegating client guard, confined state-path helper and native lease wrapper. Routed controller/item leases, artifacts, LM checkpoints, trainer staging and dataset outputs. Initial targeted security suite passes 3/3: 500 seeded invalid/valid sequences, reported expired external-lock traversal, symlinked roots/directories/leaves/cleanup gates, tripwire hashes and successor-token preservation. Compatibility and independent bypass review remain in progress."
  "2026-10-26T08:31:50.304Z",codex-agent,"Boundary-only revert proof: removed only the shared identifier validator body, leaving path confinement and production functions intact. The seeded security property failed with Missing expected exception (exit 1). Restoring the validator passes all 3 security tests. External tree-hash tripwires and the expired external review lock remain intact. Independent compatibility review also found and fixed settlement after path refusals; native recovery now expires the observed open inode/token and delegates removal to the SDK cleanup lease."
  "2026-10-26T08:41:58.536Z",codex-agent,"Compatibility checks preserve opaque content-addressed score contexts as a distinct strict schema variant; digests can never become filesystem components or native item references. SDK-only promotion keeps its existing no-process-tool path. The pinned test runner still reserves sandbox PM_PATH and rejects env-clear PM_PATH; linked tests therefore cover pure/path boundaries, while real SDK tracker tests run directly and in CI. No upstream repository changes were made."
  "2026-10-26T09:01:06.676Z",codex-agent,"Security validation complete locally: 50/50 focused evaluation and security tests, 9/9 checkpoint/staging checks, 5/5 raw-reference regressions, and the controller recovery scenarios including process takeover, worktree authority and malformed locks pass after the fixes. The 500-sequence security property additionally checks raw stored parent/approval/environment/run references and SDK relationship identifiers. Validation-only revert fails cleanly with Missing expected exception; restored security suite passes 3/3 with 100% targeted boundary-module line/branch/function coverage. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, documented declarations and zero duplication pass. Full npm/Bun release evidence will come from the PR CI checks; existing public-data evidence is retained unchanged."
  "2026-10-26T09:12:36.622Z",codex-agent,"Final path review adds typed refusal for malformed state roots (empty, non-string, NUL or more than 4096 UTF-8 bytes). Ancestor lstat checks reject links without relying on platform-specific physical-path spelling. Tripwire hashes now include directory/file modes, inodes, sizes and modification/change timestamps plus link targets; the release tripwire is a sibling of the state root. All 3 security tests still pass with 100% targeted boundary coverage. Initial CI run 40296685065 is queued; it will be superseded by the final hardening head."
  "2026-10-26T09:16:33.564Z",codex-agent,"The final transaction entry point validates transaction and step identifiers before recovery touches the workspace lock, and standalone fences validate their state root before process probing. The restored security suite passes 3/3, including 500 invalid transaction retries, with boundary-module 100% line/branch/function coverage; typecheck, test typecheck, lint and 426 documented declarations pass. Awaiting the final-head CI release matrix."
  "2026-10-26T10:26:17.970Z",codex-agent,"Completed the package-wide native-reference audit: CSV flags, stored sweep arms, transfer/evaluation references, benchmark contamination IDs and native SDK environment references validate raw identifiers. Checkpoint filenames use the shared exact SHA-256 schema, and valid digest CLI arguments retain their distinct role. The security property now includes a malformed already-registered Plan with the reported review path, positive native-ID parser round trips and cyclic-link/path-error refusals. Identifier-only and path-helper-only revert controls fail; restored security tests pass 3/3 at 100% boundary-module coverage. Sweep/transfer/security checks pass 26/26, raw-reference/CLI checks 4/4, and checkpoint compatibility checks pass after the stricter digest refusals. Full gate receipts are tracked at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/107/checks; the final PR body will record the exact head, run URL and npm/Bun counts. Implementation is complete; releasing the claim for orchestrator verification while CI runs. The item remains in progress."
  "2026-10-26T10:38:48.798Z",codex-agent,"The superseded release matrix exposed compatibility fixtures missed by narrow local checks: the Compose fixture omitted the new helper and SDK dependency; the model transported whitespace inside identifiers; corpus tests accepted symlinked roots. Updating the container fixture, retaining positive JSON/CRLF transport while asserting padded-ID refusal, and interleaving real parent-directory swaps under the new confinement contract. Coverage thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-26T10:41:19.003Z",codex-agent,"CI follow-up validation: corpus confinement tests pass 14/14, including swaps to symlinked parents after input collection; the 500-sequence SDK reference model passes with positive JSON/CRLF transport and separate typed padded-ID refusals. Aggregate byte-limit tests now use valid 200-byte IDs so both size guards remain exercised. Lease-path validation moved outside ambiguous-record parsing so typed confinement errors propagate directly. The Compose fixture now copies the shared helper and installs the pinned SDK, matching its runtime dependency; container execution remains delegated to the CI release matrix. No thresholds changed."
  "2026-10-26T11:00:32.263Z",codex-agent,"Strengthened the 500-sequence model to compare complete SDK-read native ItemDocuments, including every metadata field and full relationships, for plans, candidates and previously saved checkpoints. It uses SDK locateItem/readLocatedItem with the configured schema and type registry; no hand-written metadata normalization. The complete-document model passes 500/500 sequences locally. Typecheck, test typecheck and lint pass. Releasing the claim again; awaiting the final-head CI release matrix."
  "2026-10-26T12:14:09.307Z",codex-agent,Final-head Node 26 release gate measured 1047/1049 passing tests. Two older provenance tests still expect padded identifiers to normalize; strict intake now correctly refuses them first. Updating their contract assertions and rerunning targeted checks before a fresh full npm/Bun CI matrix. Thresholds remain unchanged.
  "2026-10-26T12:17:07.809Z",codex-agent,"Updated legacy parser and generation tests to preserve strict identifier intake: canonical ids remain valid; padded contamination/run/benchmark/environment ids and empty CSV members return rl_identifier_invalid; omitted collection-runs retains the missing-option remedy. Direct targeted provenance tests pass 2/2; npm run typecheck, npm run build:test and npm run lint pass. New linked parser command passes 1/1 via pm test --run --only-last --progress. Prior identifier/path revert controls remain recorded. Superseded CI was canceled after its Node 26 result; fresh full gates will certify the pushed test update."
  "2026-10-26T12:19:49.180Z",codex-agent,"The provenance fixture review also exposed legacy checkpoint-label normalization. Extending the same identifier schema to documented opaque artifact labels (including legacy sha256:label values), before CLI/native generation/evaluation/transfer intake. Exact digest filenames remain strict SHA-256. Adding checkpoint and base-checkpoint fields to the existing 500-sequence invalid-id property; no silent padding normalization."
  "2026-10-26T12:23:39.321Z",codex-agent,"Legacy checkpoint/policy labels now validate through the artifact variant before CLI, native generation, evaluation and transfer intake. Schema: the documented single-token alphabet with optional literal sha256: prefix, at most 200 UTF-8 bytes; true checkpoint filenames still require exact SHA-256. Expanded invalid-id property covers checkpoint/base_checkpoint/policy. Six targeted SDK/CLI/security tests and two parser tests pass; restored security suite passes 3/3 with state-boundary.ts at 100% line/branch/function coverage. Removing only identifier validation again makes the 500-sequence property fail with Missing expected exception (refusal); restoring passes. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test and npm run lint pass; new linked parser test passes through pm test --run --only-last --progress. Complete npm/Bun final-head gates remain the final verification."
  "2026-10-26T13:01:45.753Z",codex-agent,"Final-head Bun gate passed all 1049 tests with 100% line/branch/function coverage, but the unchanged statement gate found one unentered V8 block in index.ts (99.99%). Collecting targeted raw coverage to identify the remaining defensive path; no threshold or source exclusion changes."
  "2026-10-26T13:06:09.521Z",codex-agent,"Targeted raw V8 coverage identified the remaining empty-collection guard in internal generation registration. Strict CLI validation now rejects empty CSV members before that guard, while internal SDK callers still need it. Added a real-SDK intake test through an internal declaration-stripped seam: empty native collection lists refuse before environment reads/publication, and SDK readback confirms no generation was created. Kept the guard and all 100% thresholds. npm run typecheck, npm run build, npm run build:test, npm run lint and docstring gate pass (56 sources, 426 declarations)."
  "2026-10-26T13:06:51.063Z",codex-agent,"The targeted internal SDK registration regression passes 1/1, including the SDK missing-item readback. Final exact-head complete npm/Bun release gates will be linked in the PR after this coverage-only test seam update; item remains open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-26T14:35:11.026Z",codex-agent,"Re-review identified two blocking classes: raw case-preserving keys can split controller leases for one canonical SDK item, and callback path-confinement failures can escape process cleanup. Auditing all identifier-derived keys and event/stream/timer callbacks. Will add real-tracker contention properties and callback operation fault injection, record independent revert proofs, and rerun targeted/static checks plus complete npm/Bun CI gates."
  "2026-10-26T15:00:36.073Z",codex-agent,"Implemented shared SDK canonicalization before key/digest construction, including logical programme names and native approval refs, native lease/journal ids, process staging/reservations and evaluation candidate fences. The 500-pair identity property and real Race/race seed-claim race pass. The first real-child callback matrix passed 107 injected cases across 16 operation sites with zero unhandled errors, settled-once SDK history and released leases; extending explicit timer/abort and repeated stop-failure coverage before final verification. SDK 2026.10.20 does not fold NFC/NFD: tests use SDK equivalence as reference; unsafe whitespace remains a typed refusal before any lease, as round-one rules require."
  "2026-10-26T17:22:46.671Z",codex-agent,"Resumed after host OOM interruption: remote PR head and local HEAD agree at 6b2d4e4; reviewed and retained the uncommitted canonical identity and callback failure-path changes. Updated resource rules enforced: focused tests with at most two workers, no concurrent full suites. Prior callback revert timeout is not behavioral proof; a fresh isolated control removing only controllerCallback guarding now fails with the escaped stdout exception. Restored-source focused boundary verification is running."
  "2026-10-26T17:25:53.198Z",codex-agent,"Canonical identity behavioral revert proof: in an isolated source copy, changed only identifier() to return its validated raw value instead of SDK normalizeRawItemId(value). Ran node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern='canonical identity property' test/controller-boundaries.test.ts. It failed behaviorally in 0.83 seconds at the fixed Race/race case: two real native SDK leases succeeded, expected exactly one (2 !== 1). No timeout or setup failure in this control. Restored-source 500-pair property and actual concurrent Race/race controller regression passed. Strict whitespace refusal remains before SDK resolution; NFC/NFD equivalence is determined by the pinned SDK, which does not fold those forms."
  "2026-10-26T17:25:59.644Z",codex-agent,"Callback behavioral revert proof: in a separate isolated source copy, removed only controllerCallback() guarding/Promise rejection observation. Ran node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='callback wrapper' test/controller-boundaries.test.ts. The test failed with the escaped synchronous Error: stdout. Restored-source wrapper test passes for synchronous and asynchronous failures in stdout/stderr/error/close/stdin/poll/timer/abort/heartbeat/signal callbacks; the same linked command now passes through pm test --run --only-last --progress (1/1). Earlier timeout/setup controls are explicitly excluded from evidence. The production callback path reaps the child, persists one terminal settlement, and releases owned fences; heartbeat cleanup waits for pending work and rechecks ownership."
  "2026-10-26T17:29:15.828Z",codex-agent,"Review fixes verified: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/controller-boundaries.test.ts passed 128/128, zero failures/skips/cancellations, including all 122 fault cases across 16 callback filesystem sites, entry/abort/close/timer boundaries, stop failures and both real symlink scenarios; zero unhandled exceptions or rejections. Every case reads terminal job/history through the SDK, checks exactly one settlement, reaped child, released locks, unchanged external sentinel and unchanged replay. Final additional canonical reservation alias and repeated native error-event regressions pass 2/2; focused plan alias/prefix-race regressions pass 3/3. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run lint, npm run duplicates and npm run docstring pass: 56 source files, 431 documented declarations, zero clones. Both class revert proofs are recorded above. Full npm/Bun unchanged-threshold release gates will run on the pushed commit; final exact-head run URL/counts will be published in PR 107. No local full gate or concurrent full suites run."
  "2026-10-26T17:35:58.964Z",codex-agent,"Final read-only key audit found three standalone packaged trainer entry points validate job ids but ignore the SDK-canonical return, so raw case can still enter receipts and prefix artifact ledger keys. Extending the canonical identity fix there and to parsed generation collection/approval identities and completion verification before final certification. Current CI head 38ac727 is provisional; replacement exact-head gates will supersede it."
  "2026-10-26T17:39:30.528Z",codex-agent,"Canonical audit extension complete: packaged bandit, prefix and LM stdin job ids now use the SDK-canonical return before NDJSON receipts or ledger keys; parsed generation collection/approval ids, completion request/stored job ids and legacy process-body identification use the same boundary. Focused trainer/lineage regressions pass 4/4, completion/body readback regressions pass 2/2; native SDK body readback is the process-body oracle. Additional behavioral control reverting only the shipped bandit trainer function fails its canonical NDJSON job assertion; restored source passes. Typecheck, test typecheck and lint pass, zero duplication and 431 declarations remain documented. Earlier 128-case callback suite and two class controls remain valid; this extension does not change callback behavior. Superseding provisional CI head 38ac727 with these final identity sites; final exact-head npm/Bun counts will be in PR 107."
  "2026-10-26T18:14:05.983Z",codex-agent,"CI 40370837981 Node 26 completed 1178 tests: 1169 passed, nine failed, no skips/cancellations. Callback property/matrix passed. Findings: legacy raw provenance seals must be verified before canonical projection; new SDK prefix reads exposed intake snapshot timing; existing meta/improver tests still expect uppercase rejection despite required canonical acceptance; Compose tests expect the former generic trainer outcome. Also five reported uncovered branches and one cleanup callback. Fixing those concrete compatibility, timing and coverage findings before replacement full gates; retaining unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-26T18:32:43.956Z",codex-agent,"All three jobs at 5dfa3a9 reported the same 1169/1178 pass count and nine failures. Corrected the actual intake race by copying validated observations before the first await; narrow function-only revert fails eval_plan_stopping. Preserved raw historical provenance seal verification before canonical SDK semantic projection; reverting only parseGenerationSpec to the premature projection fails card_drift. Cohort labels are strictly bounded opaque data, never native item/path keys: Member/member and Unit/unit remain distinct; reverting only parseEvaluationPlan fails the new fixed-plan SDK regression. The restored citation graph regression passes. Normal unsuccessful trainer exits now return typed trainer_failure with a remedy while preserving the existing outcome and bounded improver retry; callback errors retain process_callback_failed. Improver intent and three-generation SIGKILL/replay retests pass 2/2, including uppercase CLI resume and typed unsafe-id refusal. Meta alias/reservation, fixed cohort, snapshot retests pass 3/3. Cleanup, heartbeat lost-response audit, exact-child reaping, false-stop, cohort and snapshot checks pass 6/6. Static gates pass: typecheck, test typecheck, lint, zero duplication, 431 documented declarations over 56 sources. A mixed local batch had a 600-second canonical-card property timeout and stale assertions; it is not positive evidence. The full 512-sequence property and complete npm/Bun gates will run in replacement CI under unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-26T19:12:13.714Z",codex-agent,"At df7896d, npm Node 26 and Bun each pass all 1180 tests with zero failures, skips or cancellations; all source lines and branches reach 100%. The release gate still correctly refuses 99.93% function coverage: one index.ts callback is uncalled. Adding a real CLI signal-handler fault regression for its failure sink, with native process registration instrumentation and SDK cleanup readback; thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-26T19:18:55.420Z",codex-agent,"Coverage gap closed with an actual CLI callback regression, not an exclusion or threshold change. The public command uses real non-git SDK state; native process.once registration instrumentation dispatches the installed handler in fault and ordinary modes. Both return typed loop_cancelled and SDK readback proves released seed claim, terminal cancellation audit, empty owned locks and restored signal-listener counts. Focused V8 LCOV records one hit for each of the two index.ts:4594 handler functions, including the previously untested failure sink. Typecheck, test typecheck and lint pass. Isolated function-only controllerCallback revert makes this CLI regression fail Missing expected rejection (instead of typed cancellation), with no setup error or timeout. Node 26 and Bun at df7896d each passed all 1180 tests and 100% lines/branches, but correctly failed the 99.93% function gate; those runs are superseded by the new test-only head. Final full npm/Bun counts and URL will be in PR 107."
  "2026-10-26T19:54:02.019Z",codex-agent,"At 347d08c, Bun passes all 1181 tests and Node reports 100% lines/branches/functions across the complete source scope. The independent raw V8 statement gate still refuses one process.ts block (99.99%, 1 of 7240 blocks). Extending callback fault inputs beyond Error objects: thrown null/undefined must be retained as failures rather than mistaken for the absence of failure, especially after a successful child close. Adding real-child primitive fault coverage with the same terminal/settlement/lease readback guarantees, while keeping all thresholds unchanged."
  "2026-10-26T20:07:00.694Z",codex-agent,"Primitive callback failure class closed: launchTrainer now tracks failure presence explicitly, preserving thrown undefined/null instead of treating them as no failure. Eighteen real-child cases cover stderr and successful-close callbacks with undefined, null, false, zero, NaN, both infinities, strings and symbols. All pass with typed process_callback_failed remedies, native SDK terminal history exactly once, settled reservations, reaped child PIDs, released owned locks and zero unhandled errors. Named case run: 19/19 including parent, no skips/failures/cancellations. Focused raw V8 coverage records 18 hits in the primitive error-message block. Function-only launchTrainer revert reproduces three failing cases, including callback.close/0 returning success (Missing expected rejection). The restored ordinary process suite passes 28/28, preserving materialization, aliases, budgets, recovery and native failure behavior. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, zero duplication and 431 documented declarations over 56 source files pass. Current full-gate Node26/Bun runs at 347d08c passed all 1181 tests and 100% lines/branches/functions but correctly refused the one remaining statement block; the new source and primitive-fault test will be certified by replacement full CI at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-26T21:19:16.757Z",codex-agent,"Auto round 1 reports two general invariant violations: promotion must hold every evidence/provenance target through the authoritative write, and reviewed stopping rules must be sealed chronologically before any candidate or collection. Merged the two missing origin/main commits first, preserving existing branch commits and main tracker history. Auditing all fixed/sequential/shadow promotion paths, SDK/CLI/card adoption and packed/non-git consumers; adding adversarial mutation and chronology controls without weakening existing tests. No non-blocking findings were supplied in the task text; checking available review evidence for them."
  "2026-10-26T21:35:42.784Z",codex-agent,"Class audit: all manual and recursive promotion writes share promoteGenerationCore and mutateLoopItem. The authoritative callback now collects every current SDK projection and certified absence, then acquires canonical native item leases, re-reads the exact projections through the SDK after the final acquisition, and retains all leases through the terminal write. This covers sequential review and every checkpoint, fixed results, shadow reads and ancestry without a hand-maintained dependency list. Historical reads never replace live revisions. Review chronology is enforced centrally by readEvaluationPlan against the original sealed review creation time, composing with existing plan-before-candidate and plan-before-every-Run checks. New regressions pass: 24 complete chronological permutations across three SDK/CLI surfaces (2 valid, 22 refused); seven native field mutation cases plus absent-slot and lease-release controls; all eight before/after SDK boundaries of the shared guard; actual final-checkpoint affected_version races in direct promotion and the public command, with no approval consumed, plus successful promotion while a peer is blocked by the checkpoint lease. No additional non-blocking findings were present in the supplied review or accessible PR review evidence."
  "2026-10-26T21:45:01.546Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof, revision-lock class: an isolated copy with only mutateLoopItem restored to 18cd8e6 fails both new adversarial tests with Missing expected rejection. This includes the exact final-checkpoint affected_version race through the real promotion path; the restored function publishes stale promotion instead of refusing. The active worktree retains the fix and previously passed both tests. Behavioral revert proof, chronology class: a separate isolated copy with only reviewSequentialPlan restored to 18cd8e6 fails the 24-order SDK/CLI model with Missing expected rejection for a sealed late-review plan. The restored worktree passes all 24 orders and all three surfaces. Initial isolated setup attempts lacked the existing script launcher and are explicitly excluded from proof. Native fixed-plan promotion and both manual retry/peer recovery regressions pass 3/3. Typecheck, test compilation, lint, zero duplication and 433 documented declarations over the unchanged 56-source scope pass. One file-link append used the inferred harness author; explicit codex-agent attribution is retained for subsequent writes and existing history remains append-only."
  "2026-10-26T21:52:55.078Z",codex-agent,"Class-wide follow-through found the separate close-boundary recovery path. reconcileLoopPromotion now uses the same live read set and native evidence leases, re-enforces the evaluation before closing, and resolves configured done roles through the SDK registry. Its adversarial regression reopens a valid promoted Generation, races the final checkpoint seal, and proves the Generation revision and existing consumed approval remain unchanged. Missing sealed held-out scores also refuse recovery. The packed npm archive passed the four new tests (including all chronology orders and SDK boundaries); refreshing that archive to include the recovery extension and verifying Node and Bun consumers next. Linked pure-schema test passes 1/1 via pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress; tracking is disabled by project configuration, so the explicit receipt is recorded here. Native tracker tests remain direct/CI because the linked sandbox reserves PM_PATH."
  "2026-10-26T22:01:17.073Z",codex-agent,"Additional function-only recovery revert proof: restoring only reconcileLoopPromotion to its pre-fix behavior (retaining the internal test export) makes the new promotion regression fail Missing expected rejection on recovery. Current source retains the fix. Source audit now covers both completeLoopGeneration callers: fresh manual/recursive promotion and reconciliation of a previously committed promotion. Missing-score recovery uses the existing promoted_missing_evidence parser refusal; a redundant unreachable check was removed and the new test asserts that established typed contract. Final static checks pass: production/test typechecks, build, lint, zero duplication and 433 documented declarations. Packed Node/Bun controls are being repeated against the final archive; initial missing launcher, unsupported archive-extraction API and Bun default five-second setup/timeout failures are excluded from positive evidence."
  "2026-10-26T22:06:00.495Z",codex-agent,"Final revision guard also retains every verified historical coordinate separately from current SDK projections and re-reads both under the same native item leases; historical evidence never substitutes for live revisions. Existing malformed-review, late/missing/fixed/skipped protocol, forged/gapped/terminal checkpoint and foreign-winner controls pass 4/4 after central chronology validation. Both packed Node and Bun consumers passed the four new regressions before this final historical-coordinate extension; final packed verification and exact-head npm/Bun release checks follow. Full gate thresholds, dependency pins, native tests and source scope are unchanged. The public read-only 107-item receipt remains valid and was not recomputed or edited."
  "2026-10-26T22:07:52.198Z",codex-agent,"Final packed archive verification passes 4/4 under Node and 4/4 under Bun, zero failures, including separate current/historical SDK readback, every guard boundary, direct/CLI/recovery final-checkpoint races, positive native lease contention, malformed-score refusal and all 24 chronology orders on three surfaces. Behavioral controls for mutateLoopItem, reviewSequentialPlan and reconcileLoopPromotion each fail by assertion when only that function behavior is reverted; source remains fixed. Typecheck, test compilation, build, lint, zero duplication and 433 documented declarations across 56 sources pass. Existing fixed-plan and manual retry/peer recovery checks pass 3/3; malformed/foreign protocol checks pass 4/4; linked pure schema test passes 1/1. The review supplied two blockers and no separate non-blocking findings. Both invariant classes and the additional recovery caller are addressed. Full exact-head release gate receipts will be published in PR 107 and the final report after npm Node 22/26 and Bun Node 26 complete; no merge or release is authorized."
  "2026-10-26T22:32:48.981Z",codex-agent,"Final retry audit found a third entry point: recoverManualPromotion verified card citations but omitted current evaluation enforcement, so an already-promoted manual retry could repair publication despite a corrupted final checkpoint or invalid review chronology. Adding the common evaluation gate before any manual recovery publication and a native SDK/CLI regression. Reclaimed the item. The in-flight e4a3078 release run is provisional and will be superseded; no canceled or partial gate is acceptance evidence."
  "2026-10-26T22:36:03.346Z",codex-agent,"Manual publication recovery extension passes its actual SDK/CLI regression: a pre-corrupted final checkpoint returns eval_plan_drift before card publication, preserving the existing Generation and approval consumption. Both established successful manual retry and matching-peer recovery tests pass 2/2. A function-only recoverManualPromotion revert to e4a3078 makes the expanded native promotion regression fail Missing expected rejection; all other current fixes remain present in that isolated control. The restored source passes. Static production/test typechecks, build, lint, zero duplication and 433 documented declarations pass. Final packed Node/Bun controls now include this sixth promotion scenario; the previous release run was canceled explicitly as superseded, not counted as passing evidence."
  "2026-10-26T22:47:09.593Z",codex-agent,"Closed the remaining recovery class rather than only adding a read: withLockedPromotionEvidence now provides one lease/check/release implementation for Generation outcomes and manual card publication. Manual recovery re-reads its Generation through the SDK, checks the current sealed request and evaluation, and keeps all current/historical evidence leases through publication. Completed loop recovery validates evaluation before its done-role early return. Ten native promotion/recovery scenarios pass, including corruption before repair, a checkpoint edit during manual validation, positive checkpoint contention during repair and a peer withdrawing promotion between the caller read and recovery. Existing manual missing-publication, post-commit and matching-peer retry controls pass 3/3. Guard metadata/native field controls and every eight SDK step boundaries pass; static checks pass with 434 documented declarations across the same 56 sources. Final shared-function revert and packed Node/Bun verification follow before replacing CI."
  "2026-10-26T22:59:31.722Z",codex-agent,"Final archive passes 4/4 new regressions under Node and 4/4 under Bun, zero failures. The native promotion model now covers twelve scenarios across fresh core/CLI promotion, active and completed recursive recovery, manual publication repair, a mid-validation seal edit, lease contention, missing scores and peer withdrawal. Both Generation and card-publication writes use withLockedPromotionEvidence, reading current and historical SDK projections after all canonical leases are acquired and releasing last. Reverting only that shared helper to execute without validation makes both guard and exact checkpoint-race tests fail Missing expected rejection; the worktree retains the restored implementation. Independent review chronology, close-recovery and manual-recovery function reverts also fail by assertion. Established manual retry controls pass 3/3. Production/test typechecks, build, lint, zero duplication and 434 documented declarations across 56 sources pass. Final PR receipts will report the replacement complete npm/Bun gate; canceled run 40410141060 is superseded and excluded. Both supplied blockers and the full recovery class are handled; no separate non-blocking findings were supplied."
  "2026-10-26T23:24:52.176Z",codex-agent,"Final canonical-reference audit found verifyTiming comparing raw SDK-authored Generation parent text against the canonical incumbent, after the historical seal deliberately preserves raw provenance bytes. Adding SDK canonical semantic projection only after verifying the raw creation seal, with fixed/sequential real-SDK alias regressions. This closes the earlier one-canonical-identity requirement without changing historical hashes or opaque cohort labels. Replacement e5ef0ed release run is provisional and will be superseded by the completed class fix; no partial or canceled run is positive gate evidence."
  "2026-10-26T23:30:18.872Z",codex-agent,"Canonical semantic projection regression passes for fixed and sequential native SDK provenance whose original parent and Run references use uppercase aliases. SDK readback first proves the aliases identify the exact same items, then evaluation and promotion enforcement pass while complete Generation readback remains identical, including the raw historical hash. An isolated copy with only verifyTiming restored to e5ef0ed fails with eval_plan_drift at the raw parent comparison; the current implementation passes. This preserves historical seals and opaque cohort-label case while using SDK canonical item identity for semantic comparisons. Production/test typechecks, build, lint, zero duplication and 434 documented declarations pass. Final packed Node/Bun checks now include five new regressions; superseded CI runs remain excluded from acceptance evidence."
  "2026-10-26T23:30:50.460Z",codex-agent,"Final canonical-reference archive passes 5/5 focused regressions under Node and 5/5 under Bun, zero failures: native field/metric-note/absence/backend guards, all eight SDK step boundaries, twelve promotion/recovery paths, all 24 chronology orders across three surfaces and fixed/sequential uppercase provenance aliases with raw hashes preserved. Function-only revert proofs cover the shared lease helper, chronology review, close recovery, manual recovery and canonical timing comparison; every control fails for the intended behavior and current source passes. All required local static checks pass at unchanged thresholds. Releasing the claim before the final source push; the PR and final report will carry exact-head full npm/Bun counts and URL. No merge, release or thread replies are authorized."
